### Use with REST Client (VS Code) or HTTP Client (JetBrains).
### Full documentation: docs/api.md
@base = http://localhost:8080

### OpenAPI 3.1 document (requires API_DOCS_ENABLED=true; SwaggerUI at {{base}}/docs)
GET {{base}}/openapi.json

### Create a user. Response includes Location (new user path) and ETag: "1"
POST {{base}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json
X-Request-Id: demo-create-1

{"email": "lan@example.com", "name": "Lan Nguyen"}

### List users (paginated). limit > 100 is capped at 100; maximum offset is 10000
GET {{base}}/api/v1/users?limit=20&offset=0

### Get one user (replace id). Save the ETag header for If-Match below
GET {{base}}/api/v1/users/REPLACE_WITH_ID

### Update with a version check: replace "1" with the ETag from GET. Wrong version => 412
### (Response includes a new ETag; repeating this request returns 412)
PATCH {{base}}/api/v1/users/REPLACE_WITH_ID
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "1"

{"name": "Lan Tran"}

### Partial update without a version check: omitted fields (or null) are unchanged
PATCH {{base}}/api/v1/users/REPLACE_WITH_ID
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Lan Pham"}

### --- Error examples ---

### 422: invalid input, with errors for individual fields
POST {{base}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "not-an-email", "name": ""}

### 409: email already exists (run after the Create user request above)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "LAN@example.com", "name": "Someone Else"}

### 415: missing Content-Type (or Content-Type other than application/json)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/users

{"email": "x@example.com", "name": "X"}

### 404: malformed IDs also return 404
GET {{base}}/api/v1/users/not-a-uuid

### 503: storage temporarily unavailable (stop PostgreSQL to reproduce).
### Body: type /problems/unavailable, detail "service temporarily unavailable",
### retryAfter: 1 (seconds; a native-template constant, not a MatterControl convention).
### A 503 on POST/PATCH/DELETE does NOT mean the change was not applied: the outcome is unknown.
GET {{base}}/api/v1/users

### --- Delete (run after the error examples: 409 above requires the user to exist) ---

### DELETE does not check If-Match
DELETE {{base}}/api/v1/users/REPLACE_WITH_ID

### --- Probe ---
GET {{base}}/healthz

###
GET {{base}}/readyz

### --- MatterControl product API (cmd/mcapi, separate server; see docs/implementation/p0-zcode-execution/local-contract.md §2–§2.7) ---
@mc = http://localhost:8081

### Bearer token comes from the BFF session or a real IdP grant; never a shared token.
### Replace REPLACE_WITH_* values with actual ids from your local seed.

### Create a workspace (receipted)
POST {{mc}}/api/v1/workspaces
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN
Idempotency-Key: 01910000-0000-7000-8000-000000000001
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Local workspace"}

### Create a matter (receipted; CAS via If-Match on workspace revision)
POST {{mc}}/api/v1/workspaces/REPLACE_WITH_WS_ID/matters
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN
Idempotency-Key: 01910000-0000-7000-8000-000000000002
If-Match: "1"
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Local matter"}

### Create a requirement (receipted; no CAS)
POST {{mc}}/api/v1/matters/REPLACE_WITH_MATTER_ID/requirements
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN
Idempotency-Key: 01910000-0000-7000-8000-000000000003
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Sign the SPA","outcome":"Executed SPA countersigned by both parties"}

### Read one requirement (uniform 404 for inaccessible/nonexistent)
GET {{mc}}/api/v1/requirements/REPLACE_WITH_REQ_ID
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN

### Own-operation receipt lookup
GET {{mc}}/api/v1/operations/01910000-0000-7000-8000-000000000003
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN

### Delta brief: (t1,t2] changes vs outstanding at t2
GET {{mc}}/api/v1/matters/REPLACE_WITH_MATTER_ID/brief?t1=2026-10-27T00%3A00%3A00Z&t2=2026-10-28T00%3A00%3A00Z
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN

### Export the matter (xlsx|csv; rights rechecked at retrieval)
GET {{mc}}/api/v1/matters/REPLACE_WITH_MATTER_ID/export?format=csv
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN

### Assess a claim (not receipted). expectedAssessmentId: the id you saw, "" for a first review; absent -> 428
POST {{mc}}/api/v1/matters/REPLACE_WITH_MATTER_ID/claims/REPLACE_WITH_CLAIM_ID/assessments
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{"verdict":"ACCEPTED","rationale":"checked against the signed copy","expectedSubjectEpoch":0,"expectedAssessmentId":""}

### OWNER: record that signatures do not apply to a filing (CAS via the filing ETag)
POST {{mc}}/api/v1/matters/REPLACE_WITH_MATTER_ID/filings/REPLACE_WITH_FILING_ID/signature-applicability
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_OWNER_ACCESS_TOKEN
If-Match: "REPLACE_WITH_FILING_ETAG"
Content-Type: application/json

{"signatureNotRequired":true,"reason":"informational filing; the authority requires no signatures"}

### Bulk edit preview (EDITOR+; absent field = unchanged, "" clears owner or due)
POST {{mc}}/api/v1/matters/REPLACE_WITH_MATTER_ID/bulk/preview
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{"rows":[{"rowKey":"r1","itemId":"REPLACE_WITH_ITEM_ID","expectedRevision":1,"title":"Renamed","due":""}]}

### Bulk edit commit: one UUIDv7 key per row, resent unchanged to recover a lost answer
POST {{mc}}/api/v1/matters/REPLACE_WITH_MATTER_ID/bulk/commit
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{"attemptKey":"01910000-0000-7000-8000-0000000000a0","rows":[{"rowKey":"r1","idempotencyKey":"01910000-0000-7000-8000-0000000000a1","itemId":"REPLACE_WITH_ITEM_ID","expectedRevision":1,"title":"Renamed"}]}

### Import preview (multipart: file, sourceName, format)
POST {{mc}}/api/v1/matters/REPLACE_WITH_MATTER_ID/import/preview
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=mcboundary

--mcboundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="counsel.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

rowkey,kind,title,description,dependencies
R1,REQUIREMENT,Clearance,Obtain clearance,
A1,ACTION,Prepare package,Package ready,R1
--mcboundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="sourceName"

counsel.csv
--mcboundary--

### Invalid whole import: missing rowkey column => 400 urn:mc:bad-request, no writes.
### Detail: spreadsheet cannot be read; check the format, required columns and upload limits
POST {{mc}}/api/v1/matters/REPLACE_WITH_MATTER_ID/import/preview
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=mc-invalid-import

--mc-invalid-import
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="format"

csv
--mc-invalid-import
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="invalid.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

kind,title
ACTION,Synthetic task
--mc-invalid-import--
